# 0035 XeGfx core: hardware colour for WindowServer's display transactions, GPU clock floor for late frames
#
# Base:  XeGfx core after 0001 + 0008 + 0011 + 0020 + 0022 + 0023 + 0028
# Files: gpu/xkpi/src/i915/{xg_display_hook.c,xg_display_hook.h,xg_i915_exec.c},
#        gpu/xegfx/shim/src/xnu/xg_kext.cpp, gpu/xegfx/shim/include/xg_i915.h
# Apply: patch -p1 < patches/0035-core-pipe-colour-gt-floor.patch
# Build: XeGfx 716e17c8ae70 (build/nvgfx/build_xegfx.sh; link, KPI and shadow checks pass)
#
# Hardware colour (Night Shift, colour profiles; docs/render-compression.md):
#   - once AGDC answers the pipe's colour stages (0030), CoreDisplay stops doing colour in a GPU pass and hands the
#     linearisation, colour matrix and encoding to the display pipe with each transaction.  Nothing applied them, so
#     dragging the Night Shift slider did nothing.
#   - resident call "xgPipeColour" (struct xg_pipe_colour: pre table, post table, 3x4 matrix as float bit patterns)
#     commits them to the CRTC's DEGAMMA_LUT, CTM and GAMMA_LUT in one CRTC-only atomic commit (EDEADLK retried, the
#     joined pipe follows through i915).  Tables are resampled linearly to the LUT sizes; floats are converted with
#     integer arithmetic (0..65535 for LUT entries, S31.32 sign-magnitude for the CTM).  DSB is not used for these
#     commits.  Logs one line per commit with the sizes and the time it took (~5 ms).
#
# GPU clock floor: resident call "xgGtMin" (int set_mhz or 0 to read, int *min, int *max) reads or sets the SLPC
# minimum frequency (intel_rps_set_min_frequency) and reports the max soft limit, for the accel's late-frame floor
# (0036).  Thread context; it sleeps for the GuC request.
--- a/gpu/xkpi/src/i915/xg_display_hook.c
+++ b/gpu/xkpi/src/i915/xg_display_hook.c
@@ -1551,6 +1551,199 @@
